# Teen Project Manager - Cursor AI Rules

This is a monorepo for a teen project management system with web and mobile apps.

## Tech Stack
- Monorepo: Turborepo
- Web: Next.js 14 (App Router), Typescript, Tailwind, Shadcn/ui
- Mobile: Exp (React Native), Typescript
- Backend: Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage)
- AI: Anthropic Claude API

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript for all new files
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use async/await over promises
- Keep components small and focused
- Extract shared logic to packages/utils

## Project Structure
-apps/web - Next.js web app
-apps/mobile - Expo mobile app (to be added)
-packages/database - Supabase client and types
-packages/ui - Shared components
-pacakges/utils - Shared utilities

## Key Patterns
- Use Server Components by default in Next.js
- Keep client components minimal (add "use client" only when needed)
- All database operations go through packages/database
- Share types between web and mobile via packages/database/types.ts

## When suggesting code:
- Always include proper TypeScript types
- Add error handling for async operations
- Use Supabase RLS for security
- Keep accessibility in mind (ARIA labels, semantic HTML)

## Testing approach:
- Write code that's easy to test
- Extract business logic from UI components
- We'll add tests later, focus on clean architecture now
